<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugo March trade gap unchanged at $113 mln vs Feb.</title>
<headline>Yugo March trade gap unchanged at $113 mln vs Feb.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV TRADE	 MARCH	 FEB	    MARCH 1996</p>
<p> Exports million USD  151.0	139.0		  139.0</p>
<p> Imports		  264.0	252.0		  315.0</p>
<p> Balance		 -113.0     -113.0		 -176.0</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE FIGURES (JANUARY TO MARCH)</p>
<p> Exports million USD  454.0	283.0		  329.0</p>
<p> Imports		  947.0	634.0		  758.0</p>
<p> Balance		 -493.0     -351.0		 -429.0</p>
<p>NOTES -- March year-on-year imports fell 16.3 percent while exports rose 8.4 percent.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-March imports were up 25 percent and exports rose 37.9 percent against the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>Data refer to the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>Yugoslavia ended 1996 with a $2.26 billion trade deficit. -- Gordana Kukic, Belgrade Newsroom ++381 11 222 4254</p>
